ecialty APIs & Catalogue Generics (Ex-Commodity)","st":[{"status":"Runner-up","subtheme":"Pharma CDMO / CRDMO & API import-substitution","tag":"CDMO","theme":"Pharma & Healthcare","tier":"1"}],"thesis":"The turnaround is real but not yet declared: **highest EBITDA and PAT in 18 quarters** (₹63.5cr and ₹16.3cr), base-business revenue **₹307cr, +24%**, and **net debt down 22% (₹135cr) in a single quarter to ₹479cr / 1.9x**. Crucially, the quarter was delivered *into* a West Asia crisis that raised solvent and KSM prices and, more damagingly, made raw material **intermittently unavailable — \"sometimes our lines are shut\"**. Management quantified the distortion honestly: **~₹30cr of consolidated revenue is pure cost pass-through**, so adjusted gross margin is ~53% consolidated and **54.5% in the base business** versus 51.3% reported — i.e. the underlying margin never actually broke. Two binary events land at the **Q2 results**: the **Ibuprofen strategic review** (₹700cr of deployed capital, **~-12% EBITDA margin**, ₹10–15cr of loss per quarter) and the linked decisions on **Vizag, Pondy and the CRAMS demerger**. The CEO refuses to call it a turnaround until *\"3 to 4 quarters\"* of consistent results — an unusual and creditable reluctance.","trig":[]},"lm":"2024-07","m":2945,"mem":0,"pdd":"2024-07-08","prev_stage":1,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":92.3,"s":"SOLARA","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"553.4","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"13.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-1.5","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":""}},"s":"SOLARA"}